  "semantics": [
    "Cached rights, usable state and full offset extent precede base addition and page walks.",
    "Expand-down D/B selects the 16- or 32-bit upper bound; #SS(0) and #GP(0) remain distinct.",
    "Full FFFFFFFFh expand-up crossings require a choice for that execution; no universal host policy is inferred.",
    "Paged 32-bit linear wrap retains whole-operand publication, earlier A/D effects, precise #PF/CR2 and distinct physical-backing failures.",
    "Concrete CS/ES/SS RAO, compact-memory and four-source bindings expire after one operation. Zero masks suppress accesses; unbound active operations still refuse.",
    "The concrete compact-store model retains earlier completed elements on later backing failure."
  ],
  "oracle": {
